    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nTo make a created owner return `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. Since the DTOs are generated from this spec by the OpenAPI generator, this produces a `displayName` field (with getter/setter) on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value directly from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nThe field is derived (read-only) from the persisted `firstName`/`lastName`, so it flows through both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}` without touching the persistence model or the controller logic.\n\nFull test suite is green: **11 tests, 0 failures/errors**, including the new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName`.",
